                <pb facs="0196" n="98" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg98"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1111 Gemmell, Nina E./3: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-03-31T16:00:00+08:00">March 31, 1930—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 31—11:20 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>239. Hankow’s March 30, 8 p.m., and Shanghai’s March 30, 11 a.m.<anchor n="79"
                        xml:id="d58-f1"/> Following telegram sent the Minister for Foreign Affairs
                    today is being repeated to Hankow and Shanghai: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“March 31. I have the honor to state that Miss N[ina] Earl [<hi
                                rendition="#italic">Eleanor</hi>] Gemmell, American, is reported
                            captured by Communists at Yuanchow, Kiangsi, and that other members of
                            the mission are reported confined in Yuanchow which has been taken by
                            Communists. It is requested that Your Excellency will be good enough to
                            devise immediate liaison for the release of the Americans
                            concerned.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
